Vita: measurement only. The painter profile (platform/vita/runtime/painter_profile.cpp, full
receipts, one painted frame in four) now times the parts of every J3D material packet's draw: the
material's load, its display list, the vertex arrays and format, and the shapes; inside the shapes,
each shape's prepareDraw, its format, arrays and pipeline, its matrix loads and its geometry calls.
The object lists are the largest block of the main thread's frame in the villages (10 to 12 ms of
47 in Ordon centre on the console, 12 Nov) and had never been split. The parts come out in the
paintprof_hud receipts under names starting with "j3d:". On frames that are not sampled the begin
call returns 0 and nothing is timed. No game call, order or result changes.

--- a/libs/JSystem/src/J3DGraphBase/J3DPacket.cpp
+++ b/libs/JSystem/src/J3DGraphBase/J3DPacket.cpp
@@ -210,12 +210,35 @@ bool J3DMatPacket::isSame(J3DMatPacket* pOther) const {
     return mMaterialID == pOther->mMaterialID && (mMaterialID & 0x80000000) == 0;
